  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hydroponics Innovation SADO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project is part of the scale up implemented in the period 1 July to 31 December 2023. This phase will target the same communities targeted in phase one with a focus on new and existing households.

The phase 2 of the project will be anchored the following objectives:

1. Increase access to nutritious animal feed for pastoralist communities in Somalia by promoting and scaling up the adoption of hydroponic fodder production systems.
2. Improve the health and productivity of livestock by providing a consistent supply of high-quality feed, especially during drought periods.
3. Enhance household food security by increasing milk and meat production from healthier and more productive livestock.
4. Empower pastoralist communities by equippingthem with the knowledge and skillsto operate and maintain hydroponic fodder systems, promoting self-sufficiency and resilience

The project target group and users are pastoralists in Somalia (Baidoa, Adado, Bardera, and Jariiban districts), who heavilyrely on livestock for their livelihoods. Theywould be responsible for setting up the hydroponic units, growing and harvesting the hydroponic fodder to feed their animals. The project aims to target both female and male-headed households at a ratio of 1:1whenever possible. In instances where this is not possible, a 55:45 ratio will apply in a bid to empower more female headed households.

The target groups were included in the process ofdeveloping, using, or testing the solution through participatoryapproaches, learning by doing, cross-learning, etc. User-feedback will be collected regularly during implementation to ensure that the innovation meets the needs of innovation end users. This will involve regular consultations with the target groups throughcommunity meetings, focus group discussions, and feedback sessions to ensure continuous improvement and adaptation of the innovation.</narrative>
  </description>
